FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor, whole repo: 2.** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together hold 72.2% of the surviving lines. Reaching 80% takes 4 authors. This is line-based: the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50%. It does not measure who understands the code.

**Scope:** 18 files, 1,662 non-blank lines (1,995 with blank lines), 315 commits. Figures use `git blame -w -M -C`, and no copy-detection note shifted anyone by more than 2 points.

**Left out of the counts**
- Commit `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 291 lines) is ignored. With it counted, Fiona would show 17.5%. The bus factor stays 2 either way.
- `dependabot[bot]` is excluded (10 lines, 11 commits) and gets no credit.
- Five other commits look mechanical (ESLint setup, license reformat) and were kept, not set aside: `739dc11`, `fcd2b56`, `00d6eec`, `344ce1e`, `9c2b59d`. They hold 39 surviving lines in total.

**Top authors by surviving lines (whole repo)**

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 649 | 39.0% | 95 (30.2%) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 | 33.2% | 143 (45.4%) |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 80 | 4.8% | 2 |
| Jon Church | 59 | 3.5% | 3 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 | 3.4% | 2 |

52 more authors hold 6.7% together. The largest of them is Eric di Domenico at 0.7%.

**Identity guesses (nothing written to `.mailmap`)**
- Troy Goode appears under `<email redacted>` (605 lines, 93 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (2 commits, 44 lines). The 649 above merges them. This is a guess from the matching name. Unmerged, the gmail address alone holds 605 lines (36.4%).
- `alex94puchades` shares an address with Alejandro Caravaca Puchades, so the tool counted them as one person (30 lines, 1.8%).

**Single-contributor areas**

By directory (merge of Troy's addresses assumed):

| Directory | Lines | Bus factor | Holder |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/` (only `index.js`) | 214 | **1** | Troy Goode, 67.3% |
| `test/` | 820 | **1** | Troy Goode, 51.2%. Douglas is at 42.0%, so this depends on the merge guess. |
| repo root | 323 | 2 | Douglas 29.4% and Troy 26.3%. Jon Church holds 18.3%, mostly of the README. |
| `.github/` | 305 | 2 | Douglas 30.2% and Íñigo 26.2% |

By file (one owner holds more than 80%, or all of it):
- `test/vary.js` — Troy Goode, 100%
- `.github/workflows/codeql.yml` — Sebastian Beltran, 100%
- `.github/dependabot.yml` — Ulises Gascón, 100%
- `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` — Íñigo Marquínez Prado, 98.4%
- `LICENSE` — Douglas Christopher Wilson, 94.4%
- `.eslintrc.yml`, `test/.eslintrc.yml`, `test/support/env.js` — Douglas Christopher Wilson, 100%
- `test/error-response.js` — Troy Goode, 82.7%
- `test/example-app.js` and `test/issue-2.js` — Troy Goode, 80% each
- `HISTORY.md` — Douglas Christopher Wilson, 80.5%

No owner holds half in 3 files: `README.md` (Troy 33.5%, Jon Church 27.8%), `lib/index.js` is not one of them, but `test/test.js` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` are close to it (Douglas 49.8% and 52.0%).

**Who the people are**
- **Troy Goode** holds the core library, `lib/index.js`, and most test files. His last commit was 2026-04-10.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** holds the most commits, but his last one was 2021-09-07. He is the second half of the bus factor of 2. If he is no longer active, Troy alone is the realistic maintainer of both the library and its tests.
- The CI workflow files each depend on one person: Sebastian Beltran, Íñigo Marquínez Prado and Ulises Gascón.

**Limits:** These figures show who wrote the lines that remain. They say nothing about code quality, review work, design discussions or deliberately deleted code.

